From 1a40d86a51a0b483bf124f78264d4c4cf0f78789 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 00:25:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08581/11362] [outer-loop] Phase 2a: launch expanded-roster
 gemma think-mode A/B (16 games)

ARC live-agent improvement plan Phase 2a. Adds scripts/run_exp6199_
expanded_roster.py, a thin driver reusing experiment_6199_gemma_
think_mode_ab.build_artifact() unmodified (checkpoint/resume logic
already handles the documented harness-kill risk) with a 16-game
roster (the original 12 plus r11l, sc25, s5i5, lp85) and a hard-fail
guard requiring CARNOT_ARC_INDUCE_N_CTX=32768 in the environment.

That n_ctx override is required: the module's own default (~106496,
sized for the SCORED swarm's 4-concurrent-games worst case) makes the
CUDA guard refuse a single RTX 3090 outright (needs 26624 MiB against
24576 MiB total). This driver issues induce requests strictly
sequentially, so a single slot's worth of context (32768) is correct
and sufficient -- confirmed by a live smoke test.

Smoke-testing this driver also found and fixed a genuine, previously
undiscovered confound in the underlying exp6199 script (see that
file's own commit/diff, swept into a concurrent conductor commit):
_configure_arm's no_think branch used to `os.environ.pop(...)` rather
than setting the override to an explicit "0", which silently degraded
into "both arms think" once ARC_LIVE_GENERATOR_THINK_SCORED_DEFAULT
was flipped to "1" on 2026-08-08 -- confirmed directly via a smoke
test showing reason_engaged=True on a no_think row with a genuine
<think> tag in its raw completion, then reason_engaged=False on the
same game after the fix.

The expanded run is launched in the background (setsid+nohup+disown,
GPU 1, log at the job's own tmp directory) rather than run inline,
since the original 12-game exp6199 run took ~4 hours; per-arm smoke
timings (72-254s) suggest the 16-game run will land in the low single
digits of hours. Phase 2a's own gate (>=6 discordant games favoring
think at p<0.05 on held-out exact-accuracy admission rate, clustered
per game) will be evaluated in a follow-up analysis pass once the run
completes, since the underlying script's own built-in verdict still
uses the weaker levelup_positive_recall metric Finding 3 critiqued.

